<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:13:30 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing</link><description>
Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9680d490-c804-11f1-9a9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-211506-211649-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9680d490-c804-11f1-9a9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-211506-211649-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b9d2a14-c804-11f1-9cd4-bd6088dee01f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:56:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres</link><description>
Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7652471c-c804-11f1-ac63-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-210507-211251-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7652471c-c804-11f1-ac63-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-210507-211251-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b7c5e62-c804-11f1-98f3-2dea6aa53833</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:49:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump sparks outrage over AI tiger video after sharing footage of fatal UK attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1</link><description>
Donald Trump has sparked outrage after sharing the distressing footage of a 23-year-old man with mental illness being fatally mauled by a tiger at Yorkshire Wildlife Park, captioned "Don't ever mess with nature!" This followed hours later by an AI-generated video of himself taming a tiger. The posts have been condemned as disrespectful to the victim, William Chapman, and his grieving family, who have urged people to stop sharing harrowing content of the attack. Vedika Bahl goes through it.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aaeefc0-c803-11f1-b711-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e2506ac2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aaeefc0-c803-11f1-b711-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e2506ac2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e1ceb32-c802-11f1-bb9d-433a74630947</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:39:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>How far will cockroach movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government</link><description>
It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the Cockroach movement's no longer a laughing matter for India’s government which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of youth-led mobilization that's already down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4239fb0a-c7fa-11f1-89b9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T115755Z-850024491-RC2W2OARH6QL-RTRMADP-3-INDIA-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4239fb0a-c7fa-11f1-89b9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T115755Z-850024491-RC2W2OARH6QL-RTRMADP-3-INDIA-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f84dcb48-c7f9-11f1-bdd4-9b1a8aad7837</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:40:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Growing ambitions’: Dr. Kendall on Houthis’ quest to be recognised as Yemen’s ‘legitimate' leaders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/growing-ambitions-dr-kendall-on-houthis-quest-to-be-recognised-as-yemen-s-legitimate-leaders</link><description>
What is the strategic logic behind the Houthis’ increasingly high-risk confrontation with Saudi Arabia? “Their experience in the past is that threats pay,” explains Dr. Elizabeth Kendall, Middle East specialist and President of Girton College, University of Cambridge. Dr. Kendall argues that the movement’s increasingly audacious military operations are not merely expressions of ideological hostility or Iranian influence, but calculated instruments of political coercion aimed at securing legitimacy, expanding territorial control and strengthening its negotiating leverage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f96d39c-c7ed-11f1-b60f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-161507-162732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f96d39c-c7ed-11f1-b60f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-161507-162732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fb60fa-c7ed-11f1-8501-43b1ddbf6a9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:18:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window</link><description>
Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54831ad4-c7e2-11f1-aba3-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-151217-152427-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54831ad4-c7e2-11f1-aba3-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-151217-152427-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5984c96a-c7e2-11f1-8726-872246178d56</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:51:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis threaten escalation after strike on Saudi oil giant Aramco</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-yemen-houthis-vow-continue-saudi-attacks-oil-giant-aramco-headquarters-hit</link><description>
Yemen's Houthi rebels said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco after officials in Riyadh reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's headquarters. The Iran-back militia also claimed missile strikes on the capital Riyadh and vowed to continue attacking Saudi airports and oil facilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79def022-c7e3-11f1-a49e-a91b34a35119</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:21:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>In Phoenix, young ultra-conservatives look to carry on Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy</link><description>
More than a year after the assassination of far-right influencer Charlie Kirk in September 2025, young activists from the organisation he co-founded, Turning Point USA, are working tirelessly to honour his legacy by rallying the youth vote ahead of the US midterm elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33439222-c643-11f1-b3d7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/main-89.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33439222-c643-11f1-b3d7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/main-89.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5069ad7c-c6f8-11f1-aaf1-e544774ab7eb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:37:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33439222-c643-11f1-b3d7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/main-89.png">© Studio Graphique, FMMM</source><dc:creator>Barbara GABEL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis say targeted Saudi oil giant Aramco, vow more attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-houthis-say-targeted-saudi-oil-giant-aramco-vow-more-attacks</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi Aramco, after Saudi officials reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's operations centre. Powerful explosions meanwhile rattled the Saudi capital, as the coalition fighting the Houthis said it had intercepted a missile fired by the Iran-backed group towards Riyadh.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b6e2700-c7c4-11f1-99b1-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-131055-131242-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b6e2700-c7c4-11f1-99b1-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-131055-131242-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">408ae05c-c7c4-11f1-9f5c-bd94fb508e46</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:00:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit</link><description>
King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. But the monarch, who rarely makes political interventions, emphasised Spain's need to "maintain good neighbourly relations" with Rabat after July's unprecedented migrant surge into Ceuta strained historically delicate ties. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edd0cb60-c7cd-11f1-b1d3-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-131306-131645-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edd0cb60-c7cd-11f1-b1d3-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-131306-131645-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2fcee52-c7cd-11f1-8070-654043f5fad8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:58:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine accuses SpaceX of crippling military missions as ties with US worsen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-accuses-spacex-of-crippling-military-missions-as-ties-with-us-worsen</link><description>
Ukraine accused Elon Musk's SpaceX on Wednesday of limiting Starlink services, crippling its drones, as Russian missiles knocked out power stations in attacks President Volodymyr Zelensky called "ostentatious disrespect" to Donald Trump. Kyiv's relationship with Washington has taken a sharp turn for the worse since US President Trump abruptly lifted sanctions on Russian diesel last week and publicly turned on Zelensky. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/775fbc9c-c7ce-11f1-aa9c-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-140439-140826-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/775fbc9c-c7ce-11f1-aa9c-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-140439-140826-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c5809b6-c7ce-11f1-b081-ab756fb80443</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:57:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Cornell University bans fraternity parties after alleged gang rape</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-cornell-university-bans-fraternity-parties-after-alleged-gang-rape</link><description>
Cornell University will ban parties and social events at fraternity houses until the end of the academic year, its president said on Tuesday, responding to the outcry over an alleged ​gang rape on ‌campus in 2024. The measure is the strongest reaction yet from Cornell's leadership to a lawsuit ⁠filed by a former undergraduate, Jane Doe, alleging seven men sexually assaulted her during a party. Over the last several weeks, the Ivy League school in Ithaca, New York, and its ‌president, Michael Kotlikoff, have come under heavy criticism over its response to ⁠the allegations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22e942ae-c7cf-11f1-ae0f-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-141822-142007-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22e942ae-c7cf-11f1-ae0f-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-141822-142007-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27cf59e8-c7cf-11f1-b86e-5b76a7f17b7e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:55:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>School closures persist in France as protests gain momentum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-school-closures-persist-in-france-as-protests-gain-momentum</link><description>
Some high schools in France remained closed on Wednesday, a day after tens of thousands of people joined rallies across the country to support protesting students. On Saturday, national demonstrations against the spiralling cost of living are to take place, and unions and student groups see the two protest currents fusing together.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0114342-c7d1-11f1-9625-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-143127-143305-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0114342-c7d1-11f1-9625-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-143127-143305-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a53ad2de-c7d1-11f1-b7ac-2f8ca68e4ed6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:53:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine asking US, SpaceX and NATO to clarify Starlink limitations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-asking-us-spacex-and-nato-to-clarify-starlink-limitations</link><description>
⁠Ukraine is ​in contact ​with the US, SpaceX and NATO to seek ​clarification ‌over ⁠limitations imposed on its access ‌to the Starlink satellite ⁠internet system, a source in the ​country's Defence Ministry ‌said on Wednesday. Ukrainian troops have reported that the Starlink ​connection is being shut off when travelling at ​higher speeds, causing major ​disruption to ​Ukrainian drone operations, many ​of which depend on satellite internet to pilot the craft. FRANCE 24’s International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3db4ea9a-c7d2-11f1-81c5-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-143306-143701-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3db4ea9a-c7d2-11f1-81c5-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-143306-143701-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43008018-c7d2-11f1-aee6-0576e8bf1c2e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:52:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen conflict escalates as Houthis say seized new strategic area</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-escalating-conflict-in-yemen-as-houthis-say-seized-new-strategic-area</link><description>
The Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen released footage said to show operations in the Taiz governorate. Fighting between the Houthis and forces loyal to Yemen’s internationally recognised government, backed by Saudi-Arabia, has escalated dramatically in recent weeks after the Houthis managed to seize a number of strategically important areas, according to reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41a5ac1a-c7d3-11f1-a036-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-143756-143935-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41a5ac1a-c7d3-11f1-a036-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-143756-143935-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46bd9c9e-c7d3-11f1-9932-f7c8736aae7a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:50:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Duane Davis sentenced to minimum 40 years for Tupac killing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-duane-davis-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing</link><description>
Duane Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles, United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3ec040a-c7d3-11f1-99fa-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-144148-144255-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3ec040a-c7d3-11f1-99fa-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-144148-144255-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8e90d18-c7d3-11f1-ab40-4ba6c95b857d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:48:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Dark day for Turkey': Govt takes control of most-watched news channel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-govt-takes-control-of-most-watched-news-channel</link><description>
Police raided Turkey's most-watched news channel, Halk TV, early Wednesday, halting broadcasts and installing a government-appointed administrator in the latest move against pro-opposition media. Halk TV chairman Cafer Mahiroglu condemned the move against the broadcaster's Istanbul headquarters as "a dark day for Turkey", and criticism poured in from the opposition and rights groups.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a85b8e74-c7d4-11f1-b4e9-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-152451-152648-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a85b8e74-c7d4-11f1-b4e9-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-152451-152648-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad3a69b0-c7d4-11f1-aea1-8f33ea939e17</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:47:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Guillaume Canet and Marion Cotillard reunite on the silver screen in thriller 'Karma'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261014-guillaume-canet-and-marion-cotillard-reunite-on-the-silver-screen-in-thriller-karma</link><description>
This week on arts24, our French film critic Manon Kerjean covers thrillers, history, legend and animation. "Karma" reunites exes Guillaume Canet and Marion Cotillard on screen for a thriller about a woman fleeing her past and the cult she escaped. "Moulin" follows Resistance hero Jean Moulin's final days in captivity, while "Le Fantôme de l'Opéra" returns for a modern retelling, but do critics buy it? We also discuss "Iron Boy", Louis Clichy's animated coming-of-age story inspired by his own childhood.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4548611c-c7cb-11f1-8019-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-KARMA-frame-687.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4548611c-c7cb-11f1-8019-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-KARMA-frame-687.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f786c11c-c7ca-11f1-b99f-2da53b20e916</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:34:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>French MPs back bill to tackle sexual and gender-based violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261014-french-mps-back-bill-to-tackle-sexual-and-gender-based-violence</link><description>
In France, a child is reportedly raped or sexually assaulted every three minutes. In a bid to put an end to sexual and gender-based violence, French MPs have voted for a comprehensive bill that could turn into law by the end of the year; it has yet to be debated by the more conservative Senate at the end of the month. FRANCE 24's Aurore Dupuis, who made the documentary "Broken children", tells us how this new law could help improve the situation for women and children in France.
